NC Digital creates professional logos and brand identities for small businesses across Wales — from Cardiff and Swansea in the south to Wrexham and Bangor in the north. Every logo is designed by hand, built to work at every size, and unique to your business.

> "A strong logo is the foundation of everything else. Get it right and your entire brand becomes more consistent, more credible, and more recognisable."

## Logo design built around your Welsh business

We work with businesses of every type across Wales — tradespeople, service businesses, retailers, hospitality companies, professional services firms, and start-ups. Whatever your industry and wherever you're based, we create a logo that reflects what you do and who you do it for.

Our logo design projects include:

- **Tradespeople and construction** — logos that project credibility and professionalism
- **Local retailers and hospitality** — identities that stand out on the high street and online
- **Service businesses and consultants** — clean, professional marks that build trust
- **Start-ups and new businesses** — a strong foundation for a brand that will grow

## What's included in our logo design service

Every logo project includes:

- 5 initial logo concepts covering distinct styles and directions
- Revisions until you're 100% happy with the result
- Brand colour palette — primary and secondary colours that work together
- Typography — font pairings that complement your logo and brand personality
- Brand guidelines document for consistent use across all materials
- All file formats: PNG, SVG, PDF, JPEG — ready for web, print, and large-format signage

See our full [logo design service](/services/logo-design/) for complete details.

## No AI. Designed by hand.

Every logo we create is drawn using Adobe Illustrator and Photoshop — no AI-generated artwork, no stock icon libraries, no template shortcuts. Your logo is unique to your business, designed from scratch with your brief in mind.

## Areas we cover across Wales

We design logos for businesses throughout Wales, including:

- **South Wales** — [Cardiff](/logo-design-cardiff/), [Swansea](/logo-design-swansea/), [Newport](/logo-design-newport/), [Merthyr Tydfil](/logo-design-merthyr-tydfil/), [Bridgend](/logo-design-bridgend/), [Caerphilly](/logo-design-caerphilly/), [Pontypridd](/logo-design-pontypridd/), [Llanelli](/logo-design-llanelli/), [Aberdare](/logo-design-aberdare/), [Port Talbot](/logo-design-port-talbot/), [Rhondda](/logo-design-rhondda/), [Vale of Glamorgan](/logo-design-vale-of-glamorgan/), [Penarth](/logo-design-penarth/), [Ebbw Vale](/logo-design-ebbw-vale/)
- **North Wales** — [Wrexham](/logo-design-wrexham/) and across the [North Wales region](/logo-design-north-wales/)
- **Mid Wales** — Aberystwyth, Newtown, Welshpool, and across [Mid Wales](/logo-design-mid-wales/)

## Pair it with your website

We design and build websites alongside brand identities, so your logo, colours, and typography are applied consistently from day one. View our [web design Wales service](/web-design-wales/) or [browse our portfolio](/portfolio/) to see examples of our work for Welsh businesses.

## Frequently asked questions

**How much does logo design cost?**

Contact us for a transparent, fixed-price quote with no hidden extras. Pricing depends on the scope of the project.

**How long does it take?**

Most logo projects are completed within 5–10 working days depending on how quickly feedback is provided.

**Will I own the logo?**

Yes. Full ownership of all files and designs is transferred to you on completion.

**Do you only work in South Wales?**

No — we work with businesses across Wales and the UK. We have experience working with businesses in both [North Wales](/logo-design-north-wales/) and [Mid Wales](/logo-design-mid-wales/).

**Can you design my website too?**

Yes. We offer [web design](/web-design-wales/) and [ecommerce web design](/ecommerce-web-design-wales/) alongside logo design, so your new identity can be built into a new website from the start.

See all our [web design Wales services](/web-design-wales/).
